"## Summary\n\nDevstack follow-up 32: isolation 19's F19-02.\n- **Session:**\n  - launched 17:46 EST on 2026-11-03, on #434's roadmap row `3f7dbc25`, and first delivered at 18:15;\n  - resumed at 18:20 under the orchestrator's authorization for one forced invocation, and delivered at 18:43.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 7 commits and 99 owned files, +6,548/−101: the shared e2e harness, its tests, and records under `docs/e2e/`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree at this branch's tip, merged onto current `main`. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`, with and without the `e2e` tag;\n    - `go test ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - the five `TestAPI01_Node*` tests and `TestAPI01_PublisherProofOptionalConflictVersion`;\n    - isolation's lint, build and tests. Its driver overlay compiles against the changed session type.\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...` and the committed-evidence hygiene test;\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n  - No owned Docker inventory remains. No production code, contract or AT-owned path changed.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The rule,** in `tests/e2e/node_write.go`. On exactly HTTP 412 `RESOURCE_VERSION_CONFLICT`, the shared publisher re-reads the node:\n  - if the re-read already has the intended values, the command succeeds with no further write;\n  - otherwise it retries with the fresh `ETag`, the same `Idempotency-Key` and the same body.\n- **Bounds:** at most three writes and ten seconds per command.\n  - Other statuses, other 412 codes, a failed re-read and a transport error stop at once.\n  - Go's implicit request replays and redirects are off for these writes.\n- **Why the same key is valid:** the idempotency reservation shares the action's transaction. A 412 rolls both back, and only durable successes are stored.\n- **Receipts:** every attempt and re-read, with UTC times, the sent `If-Match`, status, code and the body's SHA-256.\n- **Sites:** eight owned node writes use the helper. Four writes that no node observation can race stay unchanged.\n- **Live proof.**\n  - **First delivery:**\n    - forced invocation `e22872b7` died before enrollment, because the lane's admission wrapper put `free` into Docker's JSON output;\n    - ordinary invocation `c52b760c` passed 8/8.\n  - **The resume:**\n    - `af726b13` recovered from both 412s, but the lane's own proof check wrongly demanded a version detail. That check was fixed with a stub test; the run stays blocked, and is kept.\n    - **Forced `95fb7eab` passed 8/8.** It sent `\"0\"` on the capacity PATCH and on the publication PUT. Each got a real 412, one re-read, and a same-key, same-body retry that returned 202.\n    - Ordinary `3ad796d4` passed 8/8, with no conflict.\n- **The limit:** the API rejects the zero header before any version lookup, so the observation race isolation 19 met is not reproduced here. Isolation 20 runs its own assembled run on this publisher.\n- **Requests:**\n  - **The AT-owned node-write sites, to their owners:** isolation, secops, enrollment, members, usage and updates. Isolation's six go to isolation 20.\n  - **To the API owner:** the contract's header pattern allows `\"0\"`, and describes a current-version detail on 412. The server rejects `\"0\"` before any lookup, with empty details.\n"
